 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Words about pandemics: a vaccine (an injection that protects against a disease), vaccination, quarantine (keeping people apart who may be sick), isolation (keeping a sick person alone), a face mask, hand sanitiser, social distancing, infection, recovery (getting well again).\nSpecialists and what they treat:\n• a dentist: tooth decay and gum disease;   • an ophthalmologist: diseases of the eyes;\n• a dermatologist: skin diseases;   • a paediatrician: illnesses of children;\n• a cardiologist: heart disease;   • a gynaecologist: women's health and pregnancy;\n• an ENT doctor: the ear, nose and throat.\nMany specialist names end in -ist or -ian.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "n": "Mbah"
  },
  "problem": "{n}'s baby brother has a skin rash, and his grandmother has heart trouble. Which specialists should they see?",
  "steps": [
   "A skin rash is a skin disease: a dermatologist. (A paediatrician also treats babies.)",
   "Heart trouble is treated by a cardiologist."
  ],
  "answer": "The baby: a dermatologist (or a paediatrician); the grandmother: a cardiologist.",
  "checks": []
 },
